There is NO `ApplicationEventPublisher`, NO Spring Data `@EntityListeners`, and NO domain-event callbacks in the codebase. `OwnerRepository` is a plain custom interface (not a `JpaRepository`), and the active implementation is profile-selected.

Interface `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java:66`:

```java
    void save(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException;
```

Two implementations exist, chosen by Spring profile:

`jpa` profile — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java:44-100` (`@Repository @Profile("jpa")`), with the branch-on-id save:

```java
    @Override
    public void save(Owner owner) {
        if (owner.getId() == null) {
            this.em.persist(owner);
        } else {
            this.em.merge(owner);
        }
    }
```

`spring-data-jpa` profile — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java:36-57` (`@Profile("spring-data-jpa")`, extends `Repository<Owner,Integer>`); `save` is inherited from Spring Data's `SimpleJpaRepository` (no custom override), and only the finder queries are customized with `@Query`. (A JDBC impl also exists: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`.)

One cross-cutting side-effect around repository calls: a JMX monitoring aspect wraps every `@Repository` bean. `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/CallMonitoringAspect.java:77-95` — `@Around("within(@org.springframework.stereotype.Repository *)")`. It only measures timing/counts; it does not alter the entity. (It does not advise the Spring-Data proxy, per its own javadoc.)

