## 8. Global exception handlers / advice / interceptors

`ExceptionControllerAdvice` is the single `@ControllerAdvice`. Crucially, it also registers the `OwnerFieldsValidator` via `@InitBinder` for `OwnerFieldsDto` bodies (so it participates directly in the create-owner request binding, before the handler runs), and it maps `MethodArgumentNotValidException` (thrown by `@Valid` failures) to 400.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java` — key parts:

`:51-72` (advice class + the InitBinder that wires the owner validator):

```java
@ControllerAdvice
public class ExceptionControllerAdvice {
    ...
    private final OwnerFieldsValidator ownerFieldsValidator = new OwnerFieldsValidator();

    @InitBinder
    public void registerOwnerFieldsValidator(WebDataBinder binder) {
        if (binder.getTarget() instanceof OwnerFieldsDto) {
            binder.addValidators(ownerFieldsValidator);
        }
    }
```

`:101-104` — re-throws `AccessDeniedException` so Spring Security returns 403 rather than the generic 500:

```java
    @ExceptionHandler(AccessDeniedException.class)
    public void handleAccessDeniedException(AccessDeniedException e) throws AccessDeniedException {
        throw e;
    }
```

`:113-120` — catch-all → 500. `:130-141` — `DataIntegrityViolationException` → 404. `:150-185` — `MethodArgumentNotValidException` → 400, building a `ProblemDetail` with `schemaValidationErrors` and an `errors` list from `bindingResult.getFieldErrors()` (uses helper `BindingErrorsResponse` at `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/BindingErrorsResponse.java`):

```java
    @ExceptionHandler(MethodArgumentNotValidException.class)
    @ResponseBody
    public ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail> handleMethodArgumentNotValidException(MethodArgumentNotValidException e, HttpServletRequest request) {
        HttpStatus status = HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST;
        BindingErrorsResponse errors = new BindingErrorsResponse();
        BindingResult bindingResult = e.getBindingResult();
        ProblemDetail detail = this.detailBuild(e, status, request.getRequestURL(), ERROR_INVALID_REQUEST);
        if (bindingResult.hasErrors()) {
            errors.addAllErrors(bindingResult);
            List<ValidationMessageDto> schemaValidationErrors = bindingResult.getFieldErrors().stream()
                .map(fieldError -> { ... "Field '%s' %s (rejected value: %s)" ... })
                .toList();
            ...
            detail.setProperty("schemaValidationErrors", schemaValidationErrors);
            detail.setProperty("errors", bindingResult.getFieldErrors().stream()
                .map(fieldError -> fieldError.getField()).distinct().toList());
            return ResponseEntity.status(status).body(detail);
        }
        return ResponseEntity.status(status).body(detail);
    }
```

The extra `Validator` invoked during binding — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/OwnerFieldsValidator.java:31-47` — rejects blank/whitespace-only required fields (which the schema `@Pattern`/`@Size` do not fully catch):

```java
public class OwnerFieldsValidator implements Validator {

    private static final List<String> REQUIRED_FIELDS =
        List.of("firstName", "lastName", "address", "city", "telephone");

    @Override
    public boolean supports(Class<?> clazz) {
        return OwnerFieldsDto.class.isAssignableFrom(clazz);
    }

    @Override
    public void validate(Object target, Errors errors) {
        for (String field : REQUIRED_FIELDS) {
            ValidationUtils.rejectIfEmptyOrWhitespace(errors, field, "required", "must not be blank");
        }
    }
}
```

Security filters (interceptors/filters that apply): the filter chain is profile/property-driven. `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/BasicAuthenticationConfig.java` (active when `petclinic.security.enable=true`; enables method security `@EnableMethodSecurity(prePostEnabled=true)`, HTTP Basic, all requests authenticated, CSRF disabled) and `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/DisableSecurityConfig.java` (active when `=false`; `permitAll`). No custom `HandlerInterceptor` or servlet `Filter` beyond Spring Security exists in the project.

